short_label: IX.24
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If an even number is subtracted from an even number, then the remainder is even.
----
proof:

Let the even number *BC* be subtracted from the even number *AB.*

I say that the remainder *CA* is even.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="180" height="60" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IX.24 diagram" src="propIX24.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IX.24",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,100,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,140,0",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since *AB* is even, therefore it has a half part. For the same reason *BC* also has a half part, so that the remainder *CA* also has a half part, and *CA* is therefore even. [!just VII.Def.6]

Therefore, *if an even number is subtracted from an even number, then the remainder is even.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is used in four of the next five propositions.
